WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.605
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.605 --> 00:00:05.266
Today's message is take your shot.

00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:07.349
Over to you, Kevin Smith.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:12.293
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.293 --> 00:00:14.840
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.340
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.408 --> 00:00:20.947
- I go into the emergency
room, and I was like,

00:00:20.947 --> 00:00:22.458
"Donald Smith?" and they're like,

00:00:22.458 --> 00:00:24.678
"I'm sorry, he passed," and
they took me into the room.

00:00:24.678 --> 00:00:29.231
There's my father laying
on a gurney, just dead.

00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:31.296
He still has a tube sticking
out of him where they were

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:33.047
trying to intubate him
or something like that,

00:00:33.047 --> 00:00:35.948
but just motionless, quiet,
no breathing whatsoever,

00:00:35.948 --> 00:00:38.531
and it was weird to say the least.

00:00:38.531 --> 00:00:40.218
You always know eventually
your parents are going to go,

00:00:40.218 --> 00:00:42.529
but I wasn't ready, I wasn't
ready for that moment.

00:00:42.529 --> 00:00:45.872
And then I walked out, and I went outside

00:00:45.872 --> 00:00:47.736
and had a cigarette, I was
still a cigarette smoker

00:00:47.736 --> 00:00:49.613
in those days, and I
was just thinking about

00:00:49.613 --> 00:00:52.908
being half an orphan or
halfway to being an orphan

00:00:52.908 --> 00:00:54.301
or something like that.

00:00:54.301 --> 00:00:56.903
My brother comes out, and I was like,

00:00:56.903 --> 00:00:58.790
"Oh, can't believe it, right?"

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:00.601
He goes, "Yeah, it's pretty tough."

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:03.537
And I said, "How was it?"
because my brother was there.

00:01:03.537 --> 00:01:05.659
He was staying with my parents.

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:09.170
And Donald, without missing
a beat, my brother goes,

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:12.410
"Dad died screaming,"
and I was like, "What?"

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.101
and he goes, "Dad died screaming."

00:01:14.101 --> 00:01:15.467
I said, "What do you mean?"

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.600
He's like, "Well he woke up,
and he was kicking the sheets

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.740
"off and screaming about being
on fire, and he was so hot

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.393
"and so hot and get him
water and fucking screaming.

00:01:23.393 --> 00:01:25.431
"The screaming got louder and louder,

00:01:25.431 --> 00:01:28.508
"and it reached a fever
pitch, and he died.

00:01:28.508 --> 00:01:32.103
"And I don't know how else to
say it but dad died screaming"

00:01:32.103 --> 00:01:34.863
and that hit me like a Mac
truck, and I remember thinking,

00:01:34.863 --> 00:01:37.893
"Oh my god, in this world,
where even a good man

00:01:37.893 --> 00:01:40.153
"like my old man is
going to die screaming,

00:01:40.153 --> 00:01:42.097
"there's no point in not trying to achieve

00:01:42.097 --> 00:01:44.682
"every dream that I have."

00:01:44.682 --> 00:01:46.316
This is my eventual end.

00:01:46.316 --> 00:01:47.899
One day, that's it.

00:01:52.377 --> 00:01:56.330
And I really felt like,
man, that's like...

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:59.317
This is my future, we're all
probably going to go out screaming

00:01:59.317 --> 00:02:01.518
so the best thing to do prior to that

00:02:01.518 --> 00:02:04.099
is to try to pack that life with as much

00:02:04.099 --> 00:02:07.180
wonderfulness, fun, productivity.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.117
Surround yourself with
people that are going to

00:02:09.117 --> 00:02:11.337
help you do that because in this world,

00:02:11.337 --> 00:02:12.887
there's not a lot of support.

00:02:12.887 --> 00:02:14.945
There's a lot of negativity,
there's a lot of cynicism.

00:02:14.945 --> 00:02:17.711
Even as I sit here and tell
that story about my father dying

00:02:17.711 --> 00:02:19.893
I guarantee you there's a
cynical head in this house,

00:02:19.893 --> 00:02:21.695
maybe more, sitting
there going, "Who cares?

00:02:21.695 --> 00:02:23.215
"Move on, tell a dick joke."

00:02:23.215 --> 00:02:25.183
The world is full of why.

00:02:25.183 --> 00:02:27.522
Man, you tell people something,
they'll tell you why.

00:02:27.522 --> 00:02:29.186
Throw a rock, and you'll
hit somebody with why.

00:02:29.186 --> 00:02:30.502
Like, "Hey, man, I want to make a movie."

00:02:30.502 --> 00:02:32.099
"Why, why do you think you can do that?

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:35.522
"Why, nobody else is doing
it, why are you doing it?"

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:37.393
There's so much why.

00:02:37.393 --> 00:02:39.206
You go out and you find why not.

00:02:39.206 --> 00:02:40.636
You surround yourself with why not.

00:02:40.636 --> 00:02:41.910
People that are just like, "why not,"

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.505
when you're like, "hey, man,
I'm going to try something."

00:02:43.505 --> 00:02:44.890
They're like, "Why not,
let's give it a shot."

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:47.858
People who try to help you do
your dreams, make your dreams

00:02:47.858 --> 00:02:50.518
come true, and shouldn't
you do the same for them?

00:02:50.518 --> 00:02:52.636
We're all in this together,
and it cost nothing

00:02:52.636 --> 00:02:54.532
to encourage a artist.

00:02:54.532 --> 00:02:56.820
That's why I get up here
for almost 20 years now

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:58.900
after the movie, man, there
ain't a lot of filmmakers

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.650
get up after the movie and spend more time

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.150
than the movie itself talking,

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.734
but I've been trying to
impart one simple lesson

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:07.999
for nearly 20 years, anybody can do this,

00:03:07.999 --> 00:03:09.097
you know what I'm saying?

00:03:09.097 --> 00:03:11.236
Like, I wasn't born into a
business or the film business

00:03:11.236 --> 00:03:12.857
or born with a mic in my hands.

00:03:12.857 --> 00:03:15.696
I have no discernible
talent whatsoever, man.

00:03:15.696 --> 00:03:17.383
I have no connections to the business.

00:03:17.383 --> 00:03:19.340
We're from New Jersey and stuff.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.095
I got lucky, somebody picked up the movie

00:03:21.095 --> 00:03:23.897
and boom, I was off and running,
and part of that manifests,

00:03:23.897 --> 00:03:27.093
when you're brought into
the indie film community,

00:03:27.093 --> 00:03:31.350
part of your job, part of your
honor, part of your privilege

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:35.140
is to make sure that keeps
going to encourage other people.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:37.755
You know, to tell people
it's worth the shot

00:03:37.755 --> 00:03:40.449
just like Wayne Gretzky
said, you miss 100%

00:03:40.449 --> 00:03:42.186
of the shots you never take.

00:03:42.186 --> 00:03:44.297
It's always worth the shot.

00:03:44.297 --> 00:03:46.293
Now, if you're talking about, like,

00:03:46.293 --> 00:03:47.985
if what your shot is, you're just like,

00:03:47.985 --> 00:03:50.444
"I've always wanted to
kill 12 children, Kevin."

00:03:50.444 --> 00:03:53.063
Don't take that shot at all.

00:03:53.063 --> 00:03:55.147
I'm not talking about that, you know,

00:03:55.147 --> 00:03:56.644
I'm talking about artsy shit.

00:03:56.644 --> 00:04:00.167
You know, writing a blog, making
some music, making a movie,

00:04:00.167 --> 00:04:03.719
making a cupcake store or knitting store,

00:04:03.719 --> 00:04:05.904
or putting together a YouTube clip,

00:04:05.904 --> 00:04:09.275
just anything that's just
not, "Oh, we must do this

00:04:09.275 --> 00:04:11.438
"because it's part of my
job, or this will get money."

00:04:11.438 --> 00:04:14.703
Some shit you just do just
to see if it can be done.

00:04:14.703 --> 00:04:17.199
Live a why not life,
man, because we're all

00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:20.898
going to die screaming, so make
sure when you die screaming,

00:04:20.898 --> 00:04:22.569
you're totally fulfilled, you're like,

00:04:22.569 --> 00:04:24.009
"I took all the shots, I did it.

00:04:24.009 --> 00:04:27.029
"I went after everything I
wanted to or at least tried."

00:04:27.029 --> 00:04:30.295
Take the shot, the shot
is always worth taking.

00:04:30.295 --> 00:04:32.703
Whether it's a dopey thing like podcasting

00:04:32.703 --> 00:04:34.880
or writing a book or writing a blog.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:37.054
Think about the encouragement you get,

00:04:37.054 --> 00:04:38.575
when you encourage an artist, think about

00:04:38.575 --> 00:04:39.897
the potential that comes out of it.

00:04:39.897 --> 00:04:42.069
You tell a dude good job,
man, that person maybe one day

00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:45.124
writes that blog that you
meme out to the entire world

00:04:45.124 --> 00:04:47.795
because it says exactly what
you've always wanted to say

00:04:47.795 --> 00:04:49.786
but couldn't yourself,
or they write that song

00:04:49.786 --> 00:04:53.225
that you play over and
over after a loved one dies

00:04:53.225 --> 00:04:54.486
because it means the world to you.

00:04:54.486 --> 00:04:58.073
Or they make that movie
that is the one you cling to

00:04:58.073 --> 00:04:59.839
when everything is going wrong in life.

00:04:59.839 --> 00:05:02.612
Oh, you pop that in, and things
aren't bad for two hours.

00:05:02.612 --> 00:05:04.753
All that comes from encouraging an artist.

00:05:04.753 --> 00:05:06.786
Nothing good comes from
discouraging an artist.

00:05:06.786 --> 00:05:09.075
So for 20 years, I keep
coming up here and going,

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.632
"Go out and do it, why
the aren't you doing this?

00:05:11.632 --> 00:05:13.672
"It's so fun, you should do it."

00:05:13.672 --> 00:05:15.730
Take your shot, I took my shot,

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:19.408
and it's nothing but pussy
and donuts, you know?

00:05:19.408 --> 00:05:21.819
So I'm here to tell you,
man, give it a shot.

00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:23.069
Go out and try.

